The Solid World upon a Stage.

Hamlet, the director of all rays.
Romeo, the horizontal coordinate.
Juliet, the vertical coordinate with twice the row spacing.
Othello, the depth along the ray in quarter units.
Ophelia, the chosen solid read as a single letter.
Macbeth, the glyph offered to the audience.
Mercutio, the radial distance from the torus axis.
Benvolio, the first rotated coordinate.
Horatio, the second rotated coordinate.
Prospero, the third rotated coordinate.
Puck, the distance from the ring.
Titania, a temporary depth before the second rotation.
Portia, the first normal component or squared cube coordinate.
Rosalind, the second normal component or squared cube coordinate.
Beatrice, the third normal component or squared cube coordinate.
Cassius, the brightness of the surface.

